\item \strong{See a path on disk:} \code{\link[=open_in_explorer]{open_in_explorer()}} from the console, and
\code{\link[=addin_open_in_explorer]{addin_open_in_explorer()}} from wherever the cursor is
\item \strong{Turn pasted Windows paths into valid R:} \code{\link[=addin_paste_path]{addin_paste_path()}},
\code{\link[=addin_fix_path]{addin_fix_path()}}, \code{\link[=addin_flip_backslash]{addin_flip_backslash()}}, and
\code{\link[=addin_text_to_vector]{addin_text_to_vector()}} for a list of them
}

The \verb{addin_*()} functions are RStudio addins: call them from the \emph{Addins}
menu or the command palette (\code{Ctrl+Shift+P}), or bind them to a keyboard
